IR: Because many German men couldn't take what was happening around them, all the Nazi-- just being around with the Nazis.

INT: What city did you grow up in?

IR: Atlanta.

INT: Prior to the war, it was Frankfurt?

IR: Yes, Frankfurt until I was almost about three and a half.

INT: What language did you speak at home?

IR: German.

